   "detail": {
    "seconds": 6.3,
    "decision": "proceed",
    "plan": "Question: Among orders placed for delivery to Tier 3 addresses, is the RTO rate higher for COD than prepaid payments?\nMetrics: rto_rate, Shipped lines: count of sale lines with shipped_at IS NOT NULL, RTO lines: count of sale lines with rto_at IS NOT NULL\nBreakdowns: Payment type: COD when payment_method = 'COD'; otherwise prepaid\nFilters: sales.line_type = 'Sale'; customer_addresses.city_tier = 'Tier 3'\nTime window: 2025-01-01 to 2026-10-24 inclusive, by sales.placed_at\nComparison: COD versus prepaid within Tier 3 delivery addresses\nExpected result: One row per payment type, with RTO rate, shipped lines and RTO lines.\nAssumptions: Use the delivery address tier linked through sales.address_id.; Exclude the last three weeks of orders to reduce RTO reporting lag; some earlier outcomes may still be incomplete.; Following the verified payment-type definition, all non-COD methods are grouped as prepaid.; An observed difference indicates association, not proof that COD causes RTO."
   },
   "t": 6.39
  },
  {
   "type": "step",
   "step": "write_sql",
   "status": "started",
   "detail": {},
   "t": 6.4
  },
  {
   "type": "step",
   "step": "write_sql",
   "status": "done",
   "detail": {
    "seconds": 4.92,
    "attempt": 1,
    "sql": "SELECT CASE WHEN s.payment_method = 'COD' THEN 'COD' ELSE 'Prepaid' END AS payment_type,\n       (COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.rto_at IS NOT NULL)) / NULLIF(COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.shipped_at IS NOT NULL), 0) AS rto_rate,\n       COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.shipped_at IS NOT NULL) AS shipped_lines,\n       COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.rto_at IS NOT NULL) AS rto_lines\nFROM sales s\nJOIN customer_addresses a ON s.address_id = a.address_id\nWHERE s.line_type = 'Sale'\n  AND a.city_tier = 'Tier 3'\n  AND s.placed_at >= TIMESTAMP '2025-01-01'\n  AND s.placed_at < TIMESTAMP '2026-10-04'\nGROUP BY 1\nORDER BY rto_rate DESC NULLS LAST",
    "explanation": "Compares RTO rates for COD and all non-COD payment methods at Tier 3 delivery addresses. Orders from the final three weeks are excluded to reduce reporting lag; any difference is an association, not proof of causation."
   },
   "t": 11.31
